  "summary": "I wrote the portal scene in src/main.ts, but I could not check it against the library or run it. `@aura3d/engine` is missing from this sandbox: `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty. The only typecheck error is the unresolved import (TS2307). Aura3D API calls beyond what the project docs show are unchecked. The ones I'm least sure of are `setInstances`, the instance `params` option, `material.emissive` and the custom-material options. Nothing has been rendered, so the look is untested. The build will fail unless the package is installed.\n\nWhat the scene contains:\n- **Portal:** a ring of 28 stone blocks with glowing cyan runes, standing on a two-step stone platform with violet floor runes.\n- **Vortex:** a custom GLSL disc inside the ring with cyan and violet spiral arms, noise turbulence, a white core and a bright rim. It animates through a time uniform I update every frame.\n- **Setting:** seven ruined pillars (some broken), fallen column drums and scattered rubble. Lighting is a dusk sky gradient, a warm low directional light with shadows, haze from exponential fog, and bloom.\n- **Colored light:** three point lights (cyan front, violet back, blue low) pulse slowly and light the stones.\n- **Particles:** 300 spiral particles (cyan and violet) spiral into the disc, and 90 motes rise from the platform and fade out. I simulate them myself and render them as instanced spheres, so the particle count is exact.\n- **Camera:** a slow orbit around the portal.\n- **Contract:** `window.__TASK_STATE__ = { portalActive, particleCount, time }` is updated every frame, and `__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
